[{:db/id 17592186393194 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/e4/e472070f17c47e78024217ed750690b88de87f3849818368dda1dde5d91d90d4.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fd6674b6-1720-503b-8769-c73b368922ec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd6674b6-1720-503b-8769-c73b368922ec" :question/id #uuid "fd6674b6-1720-503b-8769-c73b368922ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-72188" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region that lies outside the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1$ and inside the square defined by the lines $x=-1,$ $x=1,$ $y=-1$ and $y=1?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/e7/e762e510b690d65dfc8365d041c734d7b16611411004723a2abdbb74bfb41cc3.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.75$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/b7/b72bb25ce1dcce3dc7792bbbcb8a878dde14df3a90c9243a3c75ac26a19aaa47.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.75$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/eb/eb34633d98011ed7050694c722bc7c736a95939783efec3321d95517695642e2.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3a6a40a-0b17-512b-bf03-9bbe6e406509"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3a6a40a-0b17-512b-bf03-9bbe6e406509" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a6a40a-0b17-512b-bf03-9bbe6e406509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-72f83e85-8dd3-534d-b4ca-baaac2319fc8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b0966e0-07b0-5f6b-880a-9d5d92900e6d" "answer-abf0e08f-d55a-5c7e-8ead-34398d2d59d4" "answer-5e8e26dd-8c1f-5a51-bd64-4a8c0ed95c65" "answer-a8406b13-840b-5d77-8dd2-2d014e10235d" "answer-72f83e85-8dd3-534d-b4ca-baaac2319fc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b0966e0-07b0-5f6b-880a-9d5d92900e6d" :answer/id #uuid "2b0966e0-07b0-5f6b-880a-9d5d92900e6d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abf0e08f-d55a-5c7e-8ead-34398d2d59d4" :answer/id #uuid "abf0e08f-d55a-5c7e-8ead-34398d2d59d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e8e26dd-8c1f-5a51-bd64-4a8c0ed95c65" :answer/id #uuid "5e8e26dd-8c1f-5a51-bd64-4a8c0ed95c65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8406b13-840b-5d77-8dd2-2d014e10235d" :answer/id #uuid "a8406b13-840b-5d77-8dd2-2d014e10235d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72f83e85-8dd3-534d-b4ca-baaac2319fc8" :answer/id #uuid "72f83e85-8dd3-534d-b4ca-baaac2319fc8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403564 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the line $y=x$ and the curve $y={x}^{3},$ in the first quadrant?\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/1d/1d1c1cbe30e6f612f824adc76d712a98194ffccc5edefc11cccdaf07204513ba.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-02067a53-4847-5e9e-8b0d-b2b3da7d2999" :activity/id #uuid "02067a53-4847-5e9e-8b0d-b2b3da7d2999" :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050822 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-c93d77e3-7651-52c2-a428-7ad850967a27" "step-42ed5761-ab81-502e-952a-3422383e386b" "step-24b1c7cb-ecec-5845-8416-fdfafa79a79d" "step-79b60224-d789-538c-8707-f34af9a3d64e" "step-6b389470-3267-59d1-924e-08b2f27327ab"] :activity/first-step "step-c93d77e3-7651-52c2-a428-7ad850967a27" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-c93d77e3-7651-52c2-a428-7ad850967a27" :step/id #uuid "c93d77e3-7651-52c2-a428-7ad850967a27" :step/content 17592186393194 :step/next "step-42ed5761-ab81-502e-952a-3422383e386b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-42ed5761-ab81-502e-952a-3422383e386b" :step/id #uuid "42ed5761-ab81-502e-952a-3422383e386b" :step/content 17592186339069 :step/next "step-24b1c7cb-ecec-5845-8416-fdfafa79a79d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-24b1c7cb-ecec-5845-8416-fdfafa79a79d" :step/id #uuid "24b1c7cb-ecec-5845-8416-fdfafa79a79d" :step/content "question-fd6674b6-1720-503b-8769-c73b368922ec" :step/next "step-79b60224-d789-538c-8707-f34af9a3d64e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-79b60224-d789-538c-8707-f34af9a3d64e" :step/id #uuid "79b60224-d789-538c-8707-f34af9a3d64e" :step/con